[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party, we start by calculating the total number of ways to choose 5 members from the 14-member committee. This is given by the combination formula \( \binom{14}{5} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m Next, we subtract the number of subcommittees that are all Republicans (\( \binom{8}{5} \)) and the number of subcommittees that are all Democrats (\( \binom{6}{5} \)).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m 2. Calculate the number of all-republican subcommittees:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m 3. Calculate the number of all-democrat subcommittees:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m 4. Subtract the invalid subcommittees from the total:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    2002 - 56 - 6 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=124012)[0m 
